    'Absolute rights, such as freedom from torture and slavery, cannot be limited. Most others can be limited by law. Modern limitation clauses, such as section 36 of South Africa\'s Constitution and article 24 of Kenya\'s, ask whether the limit is reasonable and justifiable in an open and democratic society, considering the importance of its purpose, the nature of the right, and whether less restrictive means exist. This is the proportionality test.',
